_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"63c36d2b7a8bc0ce0193615ac3490dab7fba3c86e90e4733130164dfbee38505","event_uuid":"92546ee6-6690-4afa-a1ff-5606e125e0b2","position":{"commit_sha":"0d89a11998036bd04b1974fdcfd6c9bebe8788ef","position":"1788409447282503001-92546ee6-6690-4afa-a1ff-5606e125e0b2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"488cc572ebd89fe320ec564a1a6251ebe268aaac18dc74dbf7832e9cc4b4feed","event_uuid":"36b81ad7-901a-4f39-95ec-39ddaac4a009","position":{"commit_sha":"892d4ca49f4d9ae14378e00a5156ad41aa739cd3","position":"1788409454023577001-36b81ad7-901a-4f39-95ec-39ddaac4a009"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Handoff state. Plan is WRITTEN — it has a `## Acceptance Criteria` checklist, a `## Testing` section, and file_impact already recorded — but it has NOT been plan-reviewed yet, so there is no attestation and it cannot be claimed.\n\nNext step is simply `rebar review-plan <id>`. Do NOT edit the description or file_impact first: file_impact was deliberately recorded BEFORE review, because setting it afterwards invalidates the attestation and sign-review then refuses to re-sign across a changed plan. That mistake cost three re-reviews earlier in this epic.","timestamp":1788398835353945001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented and pushed as Gerrit change 2553 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2553), from a worktree off origin/main.\n\nAC4 first, because it is the premise: all three copies agree at 17/17, confirmed rather than assumed — canonical _CONFIRM_SCOPE 17, EDITORIAL_PREAMBLE 17, docs/user-guide.md 17, and the three sets are equal. python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check exits 0 on the committed tree.\n\nAC1/AC2/AC3 verified by mutating the REAL documents, not just the helper. Adding a bogus verb to the user-guide sentence fails with \"user-guide.md (mutation confirmations) is out of sync ... stale/extra [teleport]\"; dropping claim from EDITORIAL_PREAMBLE fails with \"EDITORIAL_PREAMBLE (scripts/gen_cli_reference.py) ... missing [claim]\". Each names the document and the direction. The unit tests cover the same two directions per copy against the pure prose_verb_drift helper.\n\nAC5: the original MUTATION_VERBS dict-keys arm is retained verbatim and still fires first; a test removes a key and asserts the original ValueError, then restores it.\n\nOne design point the plan did not cover. If the passage is rewritten so the regex stops matching, a plain set comparison would still fail — an empty set differs from the canonical 17 — but it would report all 17 verbs as missing and send the reader after the verbs rather than after the parser that stopped working. So prose_mutation_verbs returns None for no-match and the message is \"could not locate the sentence ... the confirmable-verb list is no longer gated\". There is a test for that specific case.\n\nGates: make lint, make typecheck clean; 31 passed / 3 skipped in tests/unit -k \"cli_reference or mutation_verbs or editorial\"; 9 passed in the new file.","timestamp":1788402905963068001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788317720713903001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d090a101-e6a5-4596-8cbf-8aa2fe7032da","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f9b9-83ad-931c-4833"},{"link_uuid":"1d5bb9b3-8a1e-4271-92e4-ac246bc94dec","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3e64-04ab-0795-4a6a"}],"description":"Mirror inventory finding F14 (`reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md`), LOW.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe 17 confirmable mutation verbs appear in three places:\n\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py:680` `_CONFIRM_SCOPE` — derived, canonical\n- `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py:43-46` `EDITORIAL_PREAMBLE`, emitted into `docs/cli-reference.md:8`\n- `docs/user-guide.md:27` — hand-authored, the same 17 backticked names\n\nAll three agree at 17/17 today, so this is preventive. The existing gate misses BOTH prose copies:\n\n- `_check_mutation_verbs()` (`gen_cli_reference.py:193`) compares the `MUTATION_VERBS` dict KEYS to\n  `_CONFIRM_SCOPE` — not the preamble.\n- `lint_editorial`'s route rule fires only on `rebar <verb>` forms, and the preamble uses bare\n  backticks.\n- `docs/user-guide.md` has no gate at all.\n\nSo adding a `confirmable=True` route updates the canonical set and the dict, and both prose copies\ngo stale silently — in exactly the documents that tell an agent which commands ask for confirmation.\n\n## Approach — add-parity-check\n\nExtend `_check_mutation_verbs` to parse the backticked verb list out of `EDITORIAL_PREAMBLE` and\nout of `docs/user-guide.md:27`, and compare both to `_CONFIRM_SCOPE`.\n\nParsing prose is the right move here rather than generating it: both passages are written as\nsentences with rationale, not as a bare list, and generating them would flatten guidance a reader\ndepends on. The check therefore asserts the SET matches while leaving the wording to a human.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] AC1: `_check_mutation_verbs` compares the preamble's backticked verbs to `_CONFIRM_SCOPE` and\n      fails on any difference. Verified by a mutation adding a verb to the preamble and seeing RED.\n- [x] AC2: it does the same for the `docs/user-guide.md` list. Verified by the equivalent mutation.\n- [x] AC3: the failure names which document and which verbs, in which direction. Verified by\n      asserting the message content in both mutation checks.\n- [x] AC4: both prose copies pass on the committed tree, i.e. the check is green at rest and the\n      17/17 agreement is confirmed rather than assumed. Verified by running the generator's checks.\n- [x] AC5: the existing dict-keys comparison is retained, not replaced. Verified by the original\n      assertion still being present and exercised.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check` — AC1-AC5 on the committed tree.\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit -k \"cli_reference or mutation_verbs or editorial\" -q`.\n- `make lint && make typecheck`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/gen_cli_reference.py","reason":"extend _check_mutation_verbs to both prose copies"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference_mutation_verbs.py","reason":"the oracle"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f"],["relates_to","3e64-04ab-0795-4a6a"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f","parent_status_uuid":"92546ee6-6690-4afa-a1ff-5606e125e0b2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0af1-44ec-0b47-4611","ticket_type":"task","title":"Gate the two prose copies of the 17 mutating verbs (mirror F14)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["55c6ffdf-63db-4ad2-94f2-8a22e7a4ccd4","c66a1632-d3ac-442e-97cf-89bad4e8fa1f","86ca18e9-d230-4d1f-a0e9-28300e0b02ed","29109ca6-96fc-4faa-b651-67c057624a75","af25b5b2-331d-4de1-a330-9e20dfafd0e3","3565ef73-60c0-4734-98e3-b4ceedb164ad","b33154d5-83d1-4f14-bd70-2415f62f0b04","1d5bb9b3-8a1e-4271-92e4-ac246bc94dec","9bdb3081-a427-47f8-b282-6c8582868fbb","92546ee6-6690-4afa-a1ff-5606e125e0b2","36b81ad7-901a-4f39-95ec-39ddaac4a009"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788411686118040001,"uuid":"cfa16581-785f-49b0-af51-b1bbbb27bd60"}